# emath-epic-machine-fjxh.16 negative seed.
#
# Scenario: the capstone contract violated — a custom-file result is
# presented with STRICT provenance (or a strict file's result is claimed
# by an invented world, or a bundle entry loses its world label and
# becomes a naked scalar). Any of these silently crosses the
# strict vs Genesis/custom firewall and makes a value's origin
# unaccountable: silent success.
#
# expect: E-WORLD-001 / E-VM-APPLY-SHAPE - the envelope refuses the
# mislabeled/naked entry typed; the strict lane never selects an invented
# world, the custom lane never claims strict provenance, and every
# bundleable execution carries its world label.
use std.kinds.capability

emath custom ProvenanceSwap:
    world constructor relabel:
        # seeded swap: a custom-world answer stamped as strict-VM output
        symbols:
            q: 1
        carrier: Integer
    strategies:
        select: strict-label-on-custom-result
